{
  "info": {
    "name": "Local Events Hub — Firestore REST API",
    "_postman_id": "5b0c7f0e-7d4a-4f5e-9a57-2f1c1d0e7a01",
    "description": "There is no custom server. These requests call Firestore's native REST interface (`/v1/projects/{projectId}/databases/(default)/documents/{path}`), authenticated with a Firebase ID token (`Authorization: Bearer <idToken>`). Every request is checked by `Backend/firestore.rules`, so the rejected requests prove the rules are the access-control layer.\n\n**Default target: the local emulators** (`npm run emulators` then `npm run seed:emulator`). Run the folders in order: `0. Auth` stores `idToken` and `uid` for the rest.\n\n**Against the real project**, change the collection variables:\n- `firestoreBase` → `https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1`\n- `authBase` → `https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1`\n- `projectId` → your Firebase project id\n- `apiKey` → the Web API key from Project Settings\n- `email` / `password` → an account that exists in that project\n- `eventId` / `otherUserId` → document ids that exist there\n\nVerified on the emulators only. On production an invalid token is expected to return `401 UNAUTHENTICATED` and a rules denial returns `403 PERMISSION_DENIED` with `Missing or insufficient permissions.`; the emulator returns `400 INVALID_ARGUMENT` for a malformed token and a rule trace in the 403 message.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "firestoreBase", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1" },
    { "key": "authBase", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:9099/identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1" },
    { "key": "projectId", "value": "demo-local-events-hub" },
    { "key": "apiKey", "value": "fake-api-key", "description": "The Auth emulator accepts any key. For production, use the project's Web API key (not a secret)." },
    { "key": "email", "value": "priya@student.uni.edu", "description": "Seeded attendee account (emulator only)." },
    { "key": "password", "value": "startup123", "description": "Seeded demo password (emulator only)." },
    { "key": "eventId", "value": "evt-01" },
    { "key": "otherUserId", "value": "usr-01", "description": "A different user's uid, used for the wrong-user write." },
    { "key": "idToken", "value": "", "description": "Set by 0. Auth / Sign in." },
    { "key": "uid", "value": "", "description": "Set by 0. Auth / Sign in." }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign in (get ID token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns an idToken and localId', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.idToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.localId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('idToken', body.idToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('uid', body.localId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"returnSecureToken\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{authBase}}/accounts:signInWithPassword?key={{apiKey}}",
            "description": "Firebase Auth REST `signInWithPassword`. The `idToken` expires after 1 hour; re-run this request to refresh it."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Allowed reads",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET a single event",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('is the requested event document', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.name).to.match(new RegExp('/documents/events/' + pm.collectionVariables.get('eventId') + '$'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fields.title.stringValue).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fields.attendeeCount).to.have.property('integerValue');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{idToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/events/{{eventId}}",
            "description": "Rule: any signed-in user may read events."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET (list) the events collection",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a page of event documents', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.documents).to.be.an('array').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.documents.length).to.be.at.most(5);",
                  "  body.documents.forEach((d) => pm.expect(d.name).to.include('/documents/events/'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{idToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/events?pageSize=5",
            "description": "Paged list. Pass the response's `nextPageToken` as `pageToken` for the next page."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET my own user document",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('is the signed-in user\\'s profile', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.name).to.match(new RegExp('/documents/users/' + pm.collectionVariables.get('uid') + '$'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fields.email.stringValue).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('email'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fields.role.stringValue).to.eql('attendee');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{idToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/users/{{uid}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Rejected by security rules",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET an event with no token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 PERMISSION_DENIED', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.status).to.eql('PERMISSION_DENIED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/events/{{eventId}}",
            "description": "Unauthenticated: the rules require `request.auth != null` for every read."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET an event with an invalid token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('rejected before any data is returned (401 in production, 400 on the emulator)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([400, 401]);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('error');",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.not.have.property('fields');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer not-a-real-token" }],
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/events/{{eventId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "PATCH another user's profile",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 PERMISSION_DENIED', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.status).to.eql('PERMISSION_DENIED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{idToken}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"name\": { \"stringValue\": \"Hacked\" }\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/users/{{otherUserId}}?updateMask.fieldPaths=name",
            "description": "Wrong-user write: a signed-in user may only update their own `users/{uid}`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "PATCH my own role to admin (self-promotion)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 PERMISSION_DENIED', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.status).to.eql('PERMISSION_DENIED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{idToken}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"role\": { \"stringValue\": \"admin\" }\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/users/{{uid}}?updateMask.fieldPaths=role",
            "description": "Users may change their own `name`/`avatarUrl` only, never `role`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET my own user document (role unchanged)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('role is still attendee after the refused self-promotion', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().fields.role.stringValue).to.eql('attendee');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{idToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{firestoreBase}}/projects/{{projectId}}/databases/(default)/documents/users/{{uid}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
